# Cloudflare Pages edge headers for app.rwally.com.
#
# WHERE THIS FILE HAS TO LIVE. Pages reads _headers from the root of the SERVED
# directory, which is the build output. It therefore sits in src/ and build.mjs
# copies it to dist/_headers. A missing _headers is not an error and is not
# reported: the site simply serves with no policy at all, which looks identical
# to a working deploy.
#
# SYNTAX. A path pattern at column 0, then indented `Name: value` lines. A
# comment is a line beginning with # at column 0; Cloudflare documents comments
# only at column 0 and says nothing about indented ones, so every comment here
# sits at column 0 and the rule block below carries header lines and nothing
# else. A malformed line is ignored silently, so a header accidentally written
# at column 0 becomes a path pattern with no headers and does nothing.
#
# THE POLICY, DIRECTIVE BY DIRECTIVE.
#
# default-src 'none'
#   Deny by default. Every fetch directive not written below inherits it, so a
#   directive that is absent is 'none' and not 'anything'.
#
# script-src 'self'
#   /app.js and nothing else. No 'unsafe-inline' and no 'unsafe-eval', which
#   has one consequence worth stating because it is invisible until production:
#   an inline <script> block in index.html would be blocked with no error on
#   the page. All behaviour lives in the external file.
#
# style-src 'self'
#   /app.css and nothing else. This also blocks every style="..." attribute in
#   the document, so the markup carries none.
#
# connect-src 'self'
#   No third-party origin. The protocol is not deployed on Arc, so this page
#   makes no chain call: there is no address for it to read and no RPC to call.
#   This used to name the abandoned chain's public RPC, which made the LIVE
#   READS panel possible. Widen this only when a live read exists again to
#   point at, not before.
#
# img-src 'self'
#   The favicon. There is no other image and no data: or blob: anywhere.
#
# font-src 'self'
#   The two self-hosted woff2 faces. No font CDN, no external stylesheet.
#
# base-uri 'none' and form-action 'none'
#   There is no <base> and no <form>. Saying so costs nothing and removes two
#   injection routes.
#
# frame-ancestors 'none'
#   This page is never framed, which is the clickjacking defence a wallet
#   surface will need before it ever has a button that signs anything.
#
# X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
#   The browser honours the declared type rather than guessing one.
#
# Referrer-Policy and Permissions-Policy
#   Not required by the brief. Included because both are pure subtraction: the
#   first stops the path leaking to the explorer on an outbound click, the
#   second turns off device APIs this page does not use and must never use.
/*
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'none'; script-src 'self'; style-src 'self'; connect-src 'self'; img-src 'self'; font-src 'self'; base-uri 'none'; form-action 'none'; frame-ancestors 'none'
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Permissions-Policy: geolocation=(), camera=(), microphone=(), payment=(), usb=(), interest-cohort=()
